# .bat files are what the Windows scheduler executes. Keep their line endings
# deterministic so git never sees them as "modified" when they are not.
#
# Why this matters: core.autocrlf=true made every run see scripts/*.bat as
# dirty. daily_update.bat then stashed them, pulled, and popped -- and the pop
# conflicted with itself, writing <<<<<<< markers into the running script.
# cmd.exe cannot parse that, so the 08:00 task died silently for a whole day
# (2026-08-13). Byte-stable .bat files remove the trigger entirely.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Same reasoning for the shell scripts used by the cloud workflows.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Helper scripts the .bat files call. Same deterministic-bytes rule.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary artefacts: never convert, never diff as text.
*.joblib binary
*.db binary
*.gz binary
*.png binary

# Actions のワークフロー。run: ブロックは Linux の bash が読むので LF 固定。
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
